{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q15409415","formula":"C₂₂H₂₅NO₂","hill":"C22H25NO2","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":22.0,"H":25.0,"N":1.0,"O":2.0},"names":{"en":"JWH-302"},"descriptions":{"en":"JWH-302 (1-pentyl-3-(3-methoxyphenylacetyl)indole) is an analgesic chemical from the phenylacetylindole family, which acts as a cannabinoid agonist with moderate affinity at both the CB1 and CB2 receptors. It is a positional isomer of the more common drug JWH-250, though it is slightly less potent with a Ki of 17 nM at CB1, compared to 11 nM for JWH-250. Because of their identical molecular weight and similar fragmentation patterns, JWH-302 and JWH-250 can be very difficult to distinguish by GC-MS testing."},"fame":3,"pubchemCid":11493740,"mass":335.4,"charge":0,"smiles":"CCCCCN1C=C(C2=CC=CC=C21)C(=O)CC3=CC(=CC=C3)OC","inchikey":"XZVYWLVYUAQEIM-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"2-(3-methoxyphenyl)-1-(1-pentylindol-3-yl)ethanone","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"11493740","atoms":50,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":1.684,"y":-1.381,"z":-0.617,"el":"O"},{"x":6.283,"y":0.389,"z":1.5,"el":"O"},{"x":-2.498,"y":-0.09,"z":0.646,"el":"N"},{"x":-3.648,"y":0.681,"z":1.103,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.426,"y":1.361,"z":-0.026,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.524,"y":-1.415,"z":0.297,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.224,"y":-1.758,"z":-0.079,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.427,"y":-0.587,"z":0.059,"el":"C"},{"x":-5.625,"y":2.172,"z":0.475,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.243,"y":0.425,"z":0.509,"el":"C"},{"x":-6.323,"y":2.897,"z":-0.676,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.581,"y":-2.332,"z":0.283,"el":"C"},{"x":0.975,"y":-0.433,"z":-0.207,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.963,"y":-3.08,"z":-0.49,"el":"C"},{"x":1.662,"y":0.933,"z":0.008,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.298,"y":-3.638,"z":-0.128,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.01,"y":-4.008,"z":-0.509,"el":"C"},{"x":-7.492,"y":3.733,"z":-0.179,"el":"C"}